1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,279
This lesson maintains an existing IC
command board in a

2
00:00:03,279 --> 00:00:05,059
fictional warehouse exercise.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:09,310
The screens come from the same saved
exercise across browser sessions.

4
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,899
Begin in Call Details and verify the
Warehouse alarm

5
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:14,380
name and training location.

6
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:18,299
Active Command and Open Command Board
identify the available

7
00:00:18,299 --> 00:00:19,620
route into this incident.

8
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:21,579
Choose Open Command Board.

9
00:00:22,059 --> 00:00:25,049
Check the incident name again on Command
Board, along with

10
00:00:25,049 --> 00:00:26,649
Wallace Boden as commander.

11
00:00:27,059 --> 00:00:31,450
Before practicing, make this identity
check a habit; similar lane names

12
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:33,150
can appear on different incidents.

13
00:00:33,309 --> 00:00:36,270
Command Structure shows Search Division
and Staging.

14
00:00:36,730 --> 00:00:41,630
Squad 3 is already in Search Division;
Staging has no assigned resource.

15
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:45,519
Rotate and Requirements are review cues on
the saved assignment.

16
00:00:45,819 --> 00:00:47,899
They do not move the unit automatically.

17
00:00:48,389 --> 00:00:49,790
Scroll to Resources.

18
00:00:50,159 --> 00:00:53,950
All is selected, with Unassigned and
Assigned available beside it.

19
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:59,450
The pool contains Squad 3, Engine 51 and
the fictional Exercise Gate Marshal.

20
00:00:59,929 --> 00:01:04,579
Engine 51 names Christopher Herrmann in
its Officer or Team Lead position while

21
00:01:04,579 --> 00:01:06,610
the unit remains unassigned to a lane.

22
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:10,419
Crew membership and command allocation
describe different things.

23
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:14,120
For practice, explain that difference
before proposing a move.

24
00:01:14,439 --> 00:01:16,949
In Tactical Objectives, choose Add.

25
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:20,119
The empty section gives us a clear
starting point.

26
00:01:20,559 --> 00:01:24,960
In Add Objective, select Benchmark under
Type and enter the training

27
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:26,420
primary-search objective.

28
00:01:26,769 --> 00:01:28,210
Choose Add to save it.

29
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:32,670
A specific objective name gives the next
operator something concrete to review.

30
00:01:33,199 --> 00:01:36,690
Open the objective and use Progress to set
fifty percent.

31
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:39,760
The returned details show fifty percent
selected.

32
00:01:40,219 --> 00:01:43,859
Outcome, Close-out note and Complete
Objective describe a

33
00:01:43,859 --> 00:01:45,309
separate close-out decision.

34
00:01:45,670 --> 00:01:48,240
This exercise leaves the objective
incomplete.

35
00:01:48,629 --> 00:01:51,379
Practice updating progress without
treating an estimate

36
00:01:51,409 --> 00:01:52,740
as a completed search.

37
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:56,590
In the Needs section, use Add to open Add
Need.

38
00:01:57,079 --> 00:01:58,990
Choose Medical under Category.

39
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:04,459
Enter the training rehab need, set Qty to
two, and use Details to explain

40
00:02:04,459 --> 00:02:08,949
the gap: two fictional rehab positions at
staging, for internal tracking.

41
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:12,050
Choose Add after checking the name and
quantity.

42
00:02:12,459 --> 00:02:16,619
This example records a quantified need; it
does not request a provider

43
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:18,289
or demonstrate anyone arriving.

44
00:02:18,789 --> 00:02:19,900
Open the saved need.

45
00:02:20,330 --> 00:02:24,259
Its heading still shows an open medical
need with zero of two filled.

46
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:28,769
For practice, describe what remains
outstanding before entering a fill.

47
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:32,079
In the need details, set Fill to one of
two.

48
00:02:32,650 --> 00:02:38,029
Enter an explicit training explanation in
Note or Reason, then choose Save Fill.

49
00:02:38,409 --> 00:02:42,939
The number is a tracking entry; it is not
evidence of a person reaching staging.

50
00:02:43,319 --> 00:02:44,310
Reopen the need.

51
00:02:44,709 --> 00:02:48,230
Partial Fill and one of two now describe
the saved result.

52
00:02:48,609 --> 00:02:52,800
History attributes the change to Wallace
Boden and retains the training reason.

53
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:57,779
The board also shows the need at one of
two beside the objective at fifty percent.

54
00:02:58,130 --> 00:02:59,779
Leave the remaining gap visible.

55
00:03:00,130 --> 00:03:04,209
For practice, explain why a partial fill
should remain distinguishable

56
00:03:04,209 --> 00:03:06,160
from completing or closing the need.

57
00:03:06,370 --> 00:03:08,810
Scroll to Notes and choose Add Note.

58
00:03:09,290 --> 00:03:12,309
Give the next operator a concrete location
and scope.

59
00:03:12,729 --> 00:03:16,590
Our note keeps staging at the fictional
west gate and explicitly says

60
00:03:16,590 --> 00:03:18,469
there is no operational deployment.

61
00:03:18,969 --> 00:03:21,349
Under Visibility, select Internal.

62
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:24,809
The helper says the note is visible to
command staff only

63
00:03:25,059 --> 00:03:28,250
and that the log records who added it,
rather than its text.

64
00:03:28,649 --> 00:03:30,190
Public is a different choice.

65
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:33,459
Check the intended audience, then choose
Save.

66
00:03:33,869 --> 00:03:37,879
After reopening the board, the note
retains its Internal badge and body.

67
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:42,820
Below it, ICS Role Assignments names
Matthew Casey as Safety Officer.

68
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:46,029
That existing command role is separate
from a unit riding

69
00:03:46,029 --> 00:03:47,500
position or lane assignment.

70
00:03:47,889 --> 00:03:51,619
Practice checking the note audience before
using a shared command device.

71
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:56,499
Timers and PAR shows the existing Training
PAR reminder as overdue,

72
00:03:56,740 --> 00:03:58,169
with Acknowledge available.

73
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:02,180
Its elapsed time reflects the saved
exercise across sessions.

74
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:05,159
This recording does not acknowledge or
restart it.

75
00:04:05,539 --> 00:04:10,489
A reminder needs a deliberate operational
response; its badge alone says nothing

76
00:04:10,489 --> 00:04:11,880
about a crew member's condition.

77
00:04:12,510 --> 00:04:14,040
Now read Accountability.

78
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:18,589
The call says check-in timers are active,
but no timers are configured.

79
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:23,059
Refresh is visible, but this empty
configuration cannot demonstrate a

80
00:04:23,059 --> 00:04:25,559
successful check-in or a PAR result.

81
00:04:25,870 --> 00:04:29,750
For practice, explain which information is
missing before asking

82
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:31,500
a crew to rely on this display.

83
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:36,170
On Incident Map, check the actual Chicago
street map and Squad 3 marker

84
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:37,719
with its Search Division label.

85
00:04:38,139 --> 00:04:42,770
These are fictional training positions,
not a demonstration of device GPS.

86
00:04:43,249 --> 00:04:46,799
Pan to frame the surrounding streets, then
choose Save View.

87
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:50,659
Here the manual pan moves the marker to
the right of center.

88
00:04:51,050 --> 00:04:53,690
Reopening the incident map retains that
framing.

89
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,270
A full browser reload retains it too.

90
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:59,729
Pan and Save View were verified in this
web recording.

91
00:05:00,110 --> 00:05:04,989
Line, Area and Text are visible, but
annotation placement was not verified.

92
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:09,789
Native touch, location and offline
behavior need separate device checks.

93
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:13,239
Practice saving a useful view and checking
the returned map.

94
00:05:13,410 --> 00:05:16,030
Return to the board and scroll to Incident
Log.

95
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:21,140
Read the timestamped objective addition,
progress update and need-fill entry.

96
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,280
They connect the working cards to
attributed actions.

97
00:05:24,719 --> 00:05:28,679
The internal note has a non-public log
marker with its author; its

98
00:05:28,679 --> 00:05:30,630
body stays out of this log entry.

99
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:34,239
The map-created entry is also present
after Save View.

100
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:39,280
For handover practice, compare this
history with the saved cards, identify

101
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:43,759
the remaining one-of-two gap, and state
that the objective is still incomplete.

102
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:46,010
Leave this training command active.

103
00:05:46,450 --> 00:05:51,110
This lesson verifies recorded application
state; it does not establish a field

104
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:55,069
deployment, delivered notification or
completed accountability check.

